    <h2>What a typical install looks like</h2>
    <p>Most installs take half a day: a new 240-volt circuit from the panel, a mounted and tested charger, and a walkthrough of its app and settings. The price guide covers chargers up to 30 feet from the panel; longer runs are quoted after a quick look.</p>
    <h2>Before we come out</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Send a photo of your panel with the door open, and of where you want the charger.</li>
        <li>Tell us the car, or cars, you will charge, and how far you drive in a typical day.</li>
        <li>Check whether your utility offers a rebate or an off-peak EV rate: many do.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>Charging two cars</h2>
    <p>Two chargers do not need two big circuits. Chargers that share one circuit split the power between them, which is plenty for overnight charging and much easier on your panel.</p>
